# Raaya Global Solutions — environment variables
#
# These are set on the Vercel project (Settings → Environment Variables), not
# committed. For local development, copy this file to client/.env.local and run
# `npm run dev:api` in client/ so the serverless functions pick it up.
#
# PORT and CLIENT_ORIGIN used to live here for the standalone Express server in
# server/. That server has been removed — there is one backend now, the Vercel
# functions in client/api/ — so those variables no longer exist.

# ---- Email delivery (required for enquiries to reach the inbox) ----------
# A Gmail App Password, not the account password.
GMAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
GMAIL_PASS=your-16-char-app-password
RECIPIENT_EMAIL=raayaglobalsolutions@gmail.com

# ---- AI layer (entirely optional) ---------------------------------------
# Leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY unset and the site runs exactly as it did before the
# AI features existed: product search falls back to keyword matching, the
# assistant widget does not render, and enquiry emails send unchanged. Nothing
# breaks and nothing looks broken.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Defaults to claude-opus-5. The assistant is a public endpoint that anyone can
# talk to, so if traffic grows, claude-haiku-4-5 cuts the per-turn cost by
# roughly 5x. See the cost table in the README before deciding.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# low | medium | high | xhigh | max. Defaults to low — these are short,
# well-specified tasks, not research.
ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=low
